odie.com/category/kyoto-cuisine/"}, {"title": "www.city.ogi.lg.jp", "url": "https://www.city.ogi.lg.jp/site_files/file/2022/202201/p1fomarqa21po5n1b1urh5pafa24.pdf"}, {"title": "www.pref.nagano.lg.jp", "url": "https://www.pref.nagano.lg.jp/nambuken/jigyo/modeljigyo/kaigi/documents/kankou.pdf"}]}, "The search didn't turn up anything on 遠山かぶ (Tohyama turnip) in 粕汁 (kasujiru, sake lees soup) or where the dish originated.\n\nThe results were about other topics:\n- **Nagano's Tohyama area:** a tourism map for 遠山郷 (Tohyama district) mentions local food, but nothing about turnips or kasujiru.\n- **Kasujiru in general:** an Iwate prefecture recipe document describes kasujiru as a winter home dish in inland areas with sake breweries, but doesn't mention 遠山かぶ or its origin.\n- **Other regional dishes:** Yamagata, Akita, and Kyoto pages covered unrelated dishes.\n\nTo find the origin, a more specific search would help, such as \"遠山かぶ 郷土料理\" (Tohyama turnip local dish) or \"遠山かぶ 伝統野菜\" (Tohyama turnip heritage vegetable). Searching the Iida city or Tohyama village websites may also help."], "durationSeconds": 4.993023999999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Kr8bGtbsGNn89Jb48d8Ugr", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
